Change-Id: xzqvunpzorzszqqontnrlmumsxovmtwk

The rule was never to install dependencies and to report them to the
user. In practice the user is the list, and a report outside it is
lost, so a missing package blocked a pass with no record of what it
needed.

Now that lab-claude can install from FreeBSD-ports through doas, the
agent installs what it needs and keeps working, and sends a patch to
instance.conf so the jail declares the package from its next build.
Anything ports cannot supply still goes to the list rather than being
fetched or built some other way.
