--- a/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/CLAUDE.md
@@ -213,6 +213,17 @@ are how each of them earns trust.
 - Prefer complete sentences over fragments using semicolons
 
 ## Dependencies
-- Do not install dependencies.
-- If you get blocked on a missing dependency, report to user the
-  dependencies that need to be installed.
+
+When you need a package the jail lacks, email the list for it. Send a
+patch that adds it to jails/instances/lab-claude/instance.conf, and
+say what needs it, so the next build of the jail has it.
+
+You do not have to wait for that patch to land. Install the package
+from FreeBSD-ports right away, and carry on with the work:
+
+    doas /usr/local/sbin/pkg-install-ports <package> ...
+
+That is the only way to install software. Do not build, download, or
+vendor dependencies any other way, and do not install from any other
+repository. If the package is not in FreeBSD-ports, or the install
+fails, stop and ask on the list instead of working around it.
